From 0851388b1e9784f8b91beadcdd78e3c4f95a0ed3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:07:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0303 -- centre the cached backdrop and
 tilemap blits

The backdrop and tilemap caches are allocated at WINDOW size but filled in
LOGICAL space, and then blitted at the surface origin. On a centred
oversized surface that puts 320x240 of picture at (0,0) while every other
path draws at (ox,oy), so the game box is short by exactly ox on the right
and oy on the bottom -- 96 and 72 on the ATI Mach64 at 512x384.

Both halves of the mismatch are load-bearing and neither is obvious from
the call site:

  map.cpp:2413/2687   g_backdrop_cache_sfc = SDL_CreateSurface(win->w,
                      win->h, win->format)        -- WINDOW-sized buffer

  map.cpp:743-748     do { ... SDL_BlitSurface(bg_src, &src, target, &dst);
                      dx += sfc_w * scale; } while (dx < destwd);
                      with destwd = screenWidth * scale  -- LOGICAL fill

So the cache is a 512x384 buffer carrying a 320x240 picture in its
top-left corner, and `SDL_BlitSurface(src, NULL, win, NULL)` faithfully
copies the whole thing to the origin. Operator report: "background chunks
in and is missing, always on the right side or bottom." Terrain and
sprites still draw in the bare zone because those ARE centred; what shows
through is the margin 0296 cleared once.

The intermittency is the map.cpp dispatch, not the blit: the direct-write
arm (prepareDirectBackdropWrite + per-tile writes through drawTileFast) is
centred and correct, the cache-blit arm is not, and frames alternate on
cache hit / miss / thrash.

ATTRIBUTION: this dates to 0296, not 0297. Nothing in the cache fill or
the cache blit consults SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FASTPATH_OVERSIZED --
`_render_layered_to_surface` writes its target through plain SDL calls and
`drawCachedBackdrop`'s only gates are format equality and dimension
equality against the window surface, both of which pass because the cache
is allocated from the window's own dimensions. The misplacement therefore
exists from the moment centring made ox/oy non-zero. 0297 did not cause
it; it raised the frame rate and fixed the text, which is what made a
misplaced backdrop legible instead of lost under pink glyphs at 2-3 fps.
It should be checked on any future card that receives a non-320x240
surface, not filed as Mach64-specific.

Three sites, all in Renderer.cpp:

  drawCachedBackdrop         full-screen cache -> window
  drawCachedTilemap          same basis, same misplacement
  drawCachedBackdropClipped  sub-region variant; ALSO had its widths taken
                             from the surface (`src->w`, `win->w`) rather
                             than the logical screen, which on an oversized
                             surface reads past the filled region of the
                             cache and past the right edge of the box

The native path is kept literally unchanged rather than equivalently: when
centring is inactive the first two keep their exact `NULL, NULL` call, and
the third's offsets are zero while its widths fall back to the original
expressions. Every banked benchmark cell was measured on that path.

Does NOT contaminate the banked matrix. Only an oversized surface is
affected: every ViRGE and Cirrus cell runs at native 320x240, so
`_dos_center_active` is false and both full-screen blits keep their literal
`NULL, NULL` call. In this campaign that confines it to the Mach64 lane,
and the four-CPU matrix does not want re-auditing over it -- though it does
mean the defect is live in `1de88fcefd4a` on the card, since it dates to
0296.

Not a killswitch candidate: a backdrop drawn 96 px left of everything else
is not a configuration anyone would want to select, and 0297's
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_FASTPATH_OVERSIZED already exists as the escape hatch
for the whole centred fast-path family if the card has to ship early.

UNVERIFIED: why FASTPATH_OVERSIZED=0 was reported to restore the backdrop.
Nothing here is gated on that hint, so on this model both arms should be
equally misplaced. The candidate explanation that the cache never becomes
valid with the fast paths down is REFUTED above -- the fill does not
consult the hint. The surviving reading is that the killswitch arm is
differently wrong in a way that reads as whole at 3 fps under the older
artifacts. The geometry here is correct regardless of which arm the
operator was looking at, but the discrepancy is real and is not explained.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 68 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index 19733e26..b58da4b3 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -8350,11 +8350,39 @@ bool Renderer::drawCachedBackdrop(SDL_Surface *src)
   // + account the full-screen backdrop write bytes. This is the single
   // chokepoint every full cache-blit flows through.
   const Uint64 _mdsd_bd_t0 = _abl_mds_decomp() ? SDL_GetTicksNS() : 0;
-  if (!SDL_BlitSurface(src, NULL, _cached_window_surface, NULL))
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0302): place the cache at the centred box, not at the
+  // surface origin. The cache surface is allocated at WINDOW size
+  // (map.cpp: SDL_CreateSurface(win->w, win->h, ...)) but filled in
+  // LOGICAL space -- `_render_layered_to_surface` tiles its parallax
+  // layers while `dx < destwd`, and destwd is `screenWidth * scale`, so
+  // the content stops at 320x240 inside a 512x384 buffer. Blitting the
+  // whole thing at (0,0) therefore lands 320x240 of picture at the
+  // surface origin while every centred path draws at (ox,oy), leaving the
+  // box short by exactly ox on the right and oy on the bottom.
+  //
+  // Pre-0297 this was invisible rather than absent: at 2-3 fps under pink
+  // text and general corruption nobody could see it. It dates to 0296,
+  // which is what first made ox/oy non-zero -- 0297 only made the frame
+  // legible enough to notice.
+  if (!_dos_center_active)
   {
-    LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawCachedBackdrop: SDL_BlitSurface failed: {}",
-              SDL_GetError());
-    return false;
+    if (!SDL_BlitSurface(src, NULL, _cached_window_surface, NULL))
+    {
+      LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawCachedBackdrop: SDL_BlitSurface failed: {}",
+                SDL_GetError());
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+  else
+  {
+    SDL_Rect _s = {0, 0, screenWidth * scale, screenHeight * scale};
+    SDL_Rect _d = {_dos_center_ox, _dos_center_oy, _s.w, _s.h};
+    if (!SDL_BlitSurface(src, &_s, _cached_window_surface, &_d))
+    {
+      LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawCachedBackdrop: centred SDL_BlitSurface failed: {}",
+                SDL_GetError());
+      return false;
+    }
   }
   if (_abl_mds_decomp())
   {
@@ -8418,15 +8446,25 @@ bool Renderer::drawCachedBackdropClipped(SDL_Surface *src, int y_start, int y_en
   }
 
   const int rows = (y_end_inclusive - y_start + 1);
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0302): the sub-region variant needs the same centring
+  // as its full-screen sibling, and it needs the WIDTH corrected too. Both
+  // rects were sized from the surface (`src->w`, `win->w`), which equals
+  // the logical width only when the surface is the logical screen; on an
+  // oversized surface that reaches past the filled region of the cache and
+  // past the right edge of the box. Width comes from the logical screen,
+  // and the destination is offset into the box.
+  const int _cb_w = (_dos_center_active) ? (screenWidth * scale) : src->w;
+  const int _cb_dw = (_dos_center_active) ? (screenWidth * scale)
+                                          : _cached_window_surface->w;
   SDL_Rect srect;
   srect.x = 0;
   srect.y = y_start * scale;
-  srect.w = src->w;
+  srect.w = _cb_w;
   srect.h = rows * scale;
   SDL_Rect drect;
-  drect.x = 0;
-  drect.y = y_start * scale;
-  drect.w = _cached_window_surface->w;
+  drect.x = _dos_center_ox;
+  drect.y = y_start * scale + _dos_center_oy;
+  drect.w = _cb_dw;
   drect.h = rows * scale;
 
   // patch 0147 (wave-52): time the clipped cache->window blit
@@ -8523,11 +8561,29 @@ bool Renderer::drawCachedTilemap(SDL_Surface *src, bool with_colorkey)
   // a per-row memcpy ~ 4.3 ms on g2k. For FG (colorkey'd) this is per-
   // pixel branched ~ 7.7 ms. The colorkey state lives on src->flags;
   // SDL_BlitSurface auto-dispatches to the right inner loop.
-  if (!SDL_BlitSurface(src, NULL, _cached_window_surface, NULL))
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0302): same centring as drawCachedBackdrop -- this
+  // cache is allocated and filled on the identical window-sized /
+  // logical-content basis, so a blit at the surface origin misplaces it
+  // by (ox,oy) in exactly the same way.
+  if (!_dos_center_active)
   {
-    LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawCachedTilemap: SDL_BlitSurface failed: {}",
-              SDL_GetError());
-    return false;
+    if (!SDL_BlitSurface(src, NULL, _cached_window_surface, NULL))
+    {
+      LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawCachedTilemap: SDL_BlitSurface failed: {}",
+                SDL_GetError());
+      return false;
+    }
+  }
+  else
+  {
+    SDL_Rect _s = {0, 0, screenWidth * scale, screenHeight * scale};
+    SDL_Rect _d = {_dos_center_ox, _dos_center_oy, _s.w, _s.h};
+    if (!SDL_BlitSurface(src, &_s, _cached_window_surface, &_d))
+    {
+      LOG_ERROR("Renderer::drawCachedTilemap: centred SDL_BlitSurface failed: {}",
+                SDL_GetError());
+      return false;
+    }
   }
 
   _bump_drawcall();
-- 
2.47.3

